al elliptic equations\n\nPart of the book series: Progress in Mathematics (PM, volume 350)\n\n  * 3973 Accesses\n\n  * 38 Citations\n\n  * 5 Altmetric\n\n\n## About this book\n\nThis monograph offers a self-contained introduction to the regularity theory for integro-differential elliptic equations, mostly developed in the 21st century. This class of equations finds relevance in fields such as analysis, probability theory, mathematical physics, and in several contexts in the applied sciences. \n  2. ### The Square Root of the Laplacian\n\n     * Xavier Fernández-Real, Xavier Ros-Oton\n\nPages 1-43\n\n  3. ### Linear Integro-differential Equations\n\n     * Xavier Fernández-Real, Xavier Ros-Oton\n\nPages 45-190\n\n  4. ### Fully Nonlinear Equations\n\n     * Xavier Fernández-Real, Xavier Ros-Oton\n\nPages 191-288\n\n  5. ### Obstacle Problems\n\n     * Xavier Fernández-Real, Xavier Ros-Oton\n\nPages 289-339\n\n  6. ### Back Matter\n\nPages 341-395\n\nDownload chapter PDF\n\n## Reviews\n\n“The book ranges from introductory material for the very basic features of the operator to state-of-the-art results in the regularity theory for solutions. ... This makes the book accessible to beginners while making it an interesting read (and in some cases an inescapable one) to experts in the field.” (Nicola Abatangel, zbMATH 1567.35002, 2025)\n\n## Authors and Affiliations\n\n  * ### Institute of Mathematics, École Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne, Lausanne, Switzerland\n\nXavier Fernández-Real\n\n  * ### Departament de Matemàtiques i Informàtica, ICREA and Universitat de Barcelona, Barcelona, Spain\n\nXavier Ros-Oton\n\n## About the authors\n\nXavier Fernández-Real Girona is SNF Ambizione Fellow at EPFL. He received his PhD in Mathematics from ETH Zürich in 2020, for which he received the Dimitris N. Chorafas Prize as well as the Vicent Caselles Prize. He is the winner of the Rubio de Francia Prize from the Royal Spanish Mathematical Society and the Antonio Valle Young Researcher Award from the Spanish Society of Applied Mathematics. He is author of the book 'Regularity Theory for Elliptic PDE', jointly written with X. Ros-Oton.\n\n \n\nXavier Ros Oton is ICREA Research Professor at Universitat de Barcelona since 2020. Previously, he has been Assistant Professor at Universität Zürich, as well as R. H. Bing Instructor at the University of Texas at Austin. He has received several awards for young mathematicians in Spain, including the 'Premio Nacional de Investigación' for researchers under 40 in Mathematics and Computer Science. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRegularity Theory for Elliptic PDE – ScienceOpen (https://www.scienceopen.com/document?vid=1d6ca223-a308-4830-9c3b-75b78c9bfc93)\nciteturn536search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.8 years ago; Crawled: last week; Author(s): Xavier Fernández-Real, Xavier Ros-Oton ... This manuscript aims to provide a self-contained introduction to the regularity theory for elliptic PDE, focusing on the main ideas rather than proving all results in their greatest generality.\n\n# Regularity Theory for Elliptic PDE\n\nPreprint\n\nAuthor(s): Xavier Fernández-Real, Xavier Ros-Oton\n\nPublication date Created: 04 January 2023\n\n### Read this article at\n\nScienceOpenPublisherArXivFurther versions   \n\nDownload  \n\n  * Download PDF\n  *   *   *   * XML\n\nThere is no author summary for this article yet. Authors can add summaries to their articles on ScienceOpen to make them more accessible to a non-specialist audience.\n\n### Abstract\n\nThis manuscript aims to provide a self-contained introduction to the regularity theory for elliptic PDE, focusing on the main ideas rather than proving all results in their greatest generality. It can be seen as a bridge between an elementary PDE course and more advanced textbooks. This is a draft of the book \"Regularity Theory for Elliptic PDE\". The final version has been published in Zurich Lectures in Advanced Mathematics, EMS Press, 2022.\n\n### Author and article information\n\n###### Journal\n\nPublication date Created: 04 January 2023\n\n###### Article\n\nDOI: 10.4171/ZLAM/28\n\nArXiV ID: 2301.01564\n\nSO-VID: 1d6ca223-a308-4830-9c3b-75b78c9bfc93\n\nLicense:\n\nhttp://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\n\n###### History\n\n###### Custom metadata\n\nACM classes 35J15, 35B65, 35J05, 35J20, 35J60, 35R35\n\nJournal reference Zurich Lectures in Advanced Mathematics. European Mathematical Society (EMS), Zurich, 2022. viii+228 pp. ISBN: 978-3-98547-028-0\n\nCategories math.AP\n\nScienceOpen disciplines: Analysis--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRegularity Theory for Elliptic PDE | alphaXiv (https://www.alphaxiv.org/abs/2301.01564)\nciteturn536search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.8 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; @misc{fernándezreal2023regularitytheoryellipticpde, title={Regularity Theory for Elliptic PDE}, author={Xavier Fernández-Real and Xavier Ros-Oton}, year={2023}, eprint={2301.01564}, archivePrefix={arXiv}, primaryClass={math.AP}, doi={https://doi.org/10.4171/ZLAM/28}, url={https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.01564}, }\nSubmitted 04 Jan 2023\n\n# Regularity Theory for Elliptic PDE\n\nXavier Fernández-Real\n\nXR\n\nXavier Ros-Oton+2 more\n\n## Abstract\n\nThis manuscript aims to provide a self-contained introduction to the regularity theory for elliptic PDE, focusing on the main ideas rather than proving all results in their greatest generality. It can be seen as a bridge between an elementary PDE course and more advanced textbooks. This is a draft of the book \"Regularity Theory for Elliptic PDE\". The final version has been published in Zurich Lectures in Advanced Mathematics, EMS Press, 2022.\n\nView Paper\n\n2\n\nCite\n\n47 views\n\nv1\n\n## Citation\n\nCopy\n\n@misc{fernándezreal2023regularitytheoryellipticpde, title={Regularity Theory for Elliptic PDE}, author={Xavier Fernández-Real and Xavier Ros-Oton}, year={2023}, e