avier Fernández-Real  \nXavier Ros-Oton\n\nETH Zürich, Department of Mathematics, Raemistrasse 101,  \n8092 Zürich, Switzerland  \nE-mail address: xavierfe@math.ethz.ch\n\nUniversität Zürich, Institut für Mathematik, Winterthur-  \nerstrasse 190, 8057 Zürich, Switzerland  \nE-mail address: xavier.ros-oton@math.uzh.ch--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nXavier Fernández-Real (https://sma.epfl.ch/~xafernan/)\nciteturn536search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; xavier.fernandez-real at epfl dot ch ... Xavier Fernández-Real, Xavier Ros-Oton ... ### Regularity Theory for Elliptic PDE ... ### Regularity theory for general stable operators: parabolic equations\n\n# Xavier Fernández-Real\n\nMathematician · EPFL\n\nI am an Ambizione Fellow at EPFL.\n\nMy research focuses on PDEs and Calculus of Variations.\n\nIn particular, I have worked on elliptic and parabolic PDEs, free boundary problems, integro-differential equations, and transport equations.\n\nCV EPFL - MATH\n\n  * Email\nxavier.fernandez-real at epfl dot ch\n  * Institute\nInstitute of Mathematics\n  * Office\nMA C2 567\n  * Address\nStation 8, CH-1015 Lausanne, Switzerland\n\n## Books\n\n41.\n\n### Integro-Differential Elliptic Equations\n\nXavier Fernández-Real, Xavier Ros-Oton\n\nProgress in Mathematics, vol. 350, Birkhäuser, 2024.\n\nLast updated: 2026/05/13\n\n40.\n\n### Regularity Theory for Elliptic PDE\n\nXavier Fernández-Real, Xavier Ros-Oton\n\nZurich Lectures in Advanced Mathematics, EMS Press, 2022.\n\nAMS Book Review\n\nLast updated: 2025/09/10\n\n## Articles\n\n[Input: Search title, author, journal, or topic]\n\n### Preprints and submitted\n\n39. arXiv\n\n### Stable solutions of the Allen–Cahn equation in dimension three are one-dimensional\n\nHardy Chan, Xavier Fernández-Real, Alessio Figalli, Enric Florit-Simon, Joaquim Serra\n\nSubmitted, available at arXiv.\n\n38. arXiv\n\n### The stability conjecture for the Bernoulli problem in dimension four\n\nXavier Fernández-Real, Joaquim Serra\n\nSubmitted, available at arXiv.\n\nRead online 37. arXiv\n\n### Superharmonicity of the fractional ground state\n\nNicola De Nitti, Xavier Fernández-Real, Florian Grube, Harsh Prasad\n\nSubmitted, available at arXiv.\n\n36. arXiv\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRegularity Theory for Elliptic PDE | EMS Press (https://ems.press/books/zlam/239)\nciteturn536search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.9 years ago; Crawled: 4 weeks ago;   * ### Xavier Fernández-Real ... The question of regularity has been a central line of research in elliptic PDE during the second half of the 20th century and has influenced many areas of mathematics linked one way or another with PDE.This text aims to provide a self-contained introduction to the regularity theory for elliptic PDE, focusing on the main ideas rather than proving all results in their greatest generality.\n\n# Regularity Theory for Elliptic PDE\n\n  * ### Xavier Fernández-Real\n\nÉcole Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne, Switzerland\n\nImage: Regularity Theory for Elliptic PDE cover\n\nBuy from $55.00Download PDF\n\nA subscription is required to access this book.\n\nOne of the most basic mathematical questions in PDE is that of regularity. A classical example is Hilbert’s XIXth problem, stated in 1900, which was solved by De Giorgi and Nash in the 1950’s. The question of regularity has been a central line of research in elliptic PDE during the second half of the 20th century and has influenced many areas of mathematics linked one way or another with PDE.\n\nThis text aims to provide a self-contained introduction to the regularity theory for elliptic PDE, focusing on the main ideas rather than proving all results in their greatest generality. It can be seen as a bridge between an elementary PDE course and more advanced books.\n\nThe book starts with a short review of the Laplace operator and harmonic functions. The theory of Schauder estimates is developed next, but presented with various proofs of the results. Nonlinear elliptic PDE are covered in the following, both in the variational and non-variational setting and, finally, the obstacle problem is studied in detail, establishing the regularity of solutions and free boundaries.\n\n## Dates\n\nPublished\n    6 December 2022\n\n## Identifiers\n\nDOI\n    10.4171/ZLAM/28\nISBN print\n    978-3-98547-028-0\nISBN digital\n    978-3-98547-528-5\n\n## Keywords\n\n  * elliptic PDE\n  * Schauder estimates\n  * Hilbert XIXth problem\n  * nonlinear elliptic equations\n  * obstacle problem\n\n## Mathematics Subject Classification\n\n  * 35J15\n  * 35B65\n  * 35J05\n  * 35J20\n  * 35J60\n  * 35R35\n\n## Print\n\nSoftcover, 236 pages, 17cm x 24cm--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRegularity Theory for Elliptic PDE (https://sma.epfl.ch/~xafernan/Documents/Fernandez-Real_Ros-Oton_Book.pdf)\nciteturn536search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.1 years ago; Regularity Theory for Elliptic PDE ... Xavier Ros-Oton ... E-mail address: xavier.fernandez-real@epfl.ch\nRegularity Theory for Elliptic PDE\n\nXavier Fernández-Real  \nXavier Ros-Oton\n\nEPFL SB MATH, Institute of Mathematics, Station 8, CH-1015 Lausanne, Switzerland  \nE-mail address: xavier.fernandez-real@epfl.ch\n\nUniversität Zürich, Institut für Mathematik, Winterthurerstrasse 190, 8057 Zürich, Switzerland, &  \nICREA, Pg. Lluís Companys 23, 08010 Barcelona, Spain, &  \nUniversitat de Barcelona, Departament de Matemàtiques i Informàtica, Gran Via de les Corts Catalanes 585, 08007 Barcelona, Spain, &  \nCentre de Recerca Matemàtica, Edifici C, Campus Bellaterra, 08193 Bellaterra, Spain  \nE-mail address: xros@icrea.cat--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRegularity Theory for Elliptic PDE | Reviews | EMS Press (https://ems.press/books/zlam/239/reviews)\nciteturn536search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.9 years ago; Cra